course: dictionary
lesson: 12783
title: Efficacy: how well something works
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Efficacy is a formal word. It means how well something does the job you want it to do, especially a medicine, a treatment or a method. Think of it as the power to get the result.
explain: Scientists measure efficacy by testing a medicine carefully and checking whether it works. «The trial showed the efficacy of the new medicine.» The sentence tells you the medicine was checked to see how well it worked.
explain: Look for clues. Words like «proven», «test» and «of» often sit near efficacy. «The doctors tested the efficacy of the new cream.» Ask yourself: tested what? The answer is how well the cream works.
explain: Efficacy is a noun, and you usually say «the efficacy», not «an efficacy». To check your meaning, swap in "how well it works". If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Efficacy means the power to produce the result you want.
fact: «Efficacy» is most often used about medicines, treatments and methods.
fact: «Proven efficacy» means it has been shown, by testing, to work.
fact: «Test the efficacy» means to check how well something works.
fact: Efficacy is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in science, medicine and exam texts.
exercise: «The scientists wanted to know the efficacy of the new medicine.» What does efficacy mean here? | How much the medicine costs | *How well the medicine works | How the medicine tastes | How quickly the medicine is sold
exercise: «The trial proved the efficacy of the vaccine.» Which word means nearly the same as efficacy here? | Cost | *Effectiveness | Colour | Length
exercise: Ava says efficacy means "how nice a medicine smells". Is she right? | Yes, it is about the price | Yes, it is about the smell | *No, it means how well something works | No, it means the colour of the packet
test: «Doctors tested the efficacy of the new treatment before they used it.» What does efficacy mean here? | How loud the room was | *Whether the treatment works well | How old the doctors are | How many people wanted it
test: «The method has proven efficacy in many schools.» What does proven efficacy suggest? | *It has been shown to work | It is very old | It is hard to find | It costs a lot of money
exam: «Which of these best explains efficacy?» | The name of a doctor | The place where medicine is made | *The power to produce the result you want | The cost of a medicine
